  "term": "diabetic retinopathy",
  "definition": "Diabetic retinopathy is a retinal disease that develops as a complication of diabetes mellitus. It involves progressive damage to the retina’s small blood vessels, including changes such as aneurysms, retinal swelling, and abnormal new blood vessel growth in the eye.",
